  "nonlinear_category": "ZIGZAG",
  "nonlinear_category_reason": "Two periods a quarter of a century apart alternate through the book, each moving forward, and every present-day scene is answered by the day in the earlier period that produced it.",
  "syuzhet_notes": "The telling alternates between the fortnight around the cousin's death and the return a quarter of a century afterwards, drifting between them mid-paragraph. Both strands run forward, and the book closes on the earliest scene of the affair, so the last thing the reader is given is the beginning.",
  "fabula_notes": "Chronology is recoverable from the ages of the twins and from the cousin's death, which the book dates precisely. The prose withholds the drowning and the killing until late but never places them ambiguously.",
